# Git merge drivers — SCOPED TRIAL (agent-infra only). Provenance: git-ecosystem
# survey 2026-06-19. Two drivers:
#   mergiraf — AST/tree-sitter-aware merge: auto-resolves STRUCTURAL conflicts,
#              falls back to ordinary conflict markers when unsafe (never hides a
#              real conflict). Binary: `brew install mergiraf`; driver defined in
#              .git/config (local). Until that driver is configured, git silently
#              falls back to the default merge for these paths (so this is safe to
#              commit ahead of the driver).
#   union    — keep BOTH sides' lines on conflict; correct for append-only ledgers
#              (the worktree / peer-session merge pain).

# AST-aware merge for code + single-doc structured files
*.py    merge=mergiraf
*.js    merge=mergiraf
*.ts    merge=mergiraf
*.json  merge=mergiraf
*.toml  merge=mergiraf
*.yaml  merge=mergiraf
*.yml   merge=mergiraf

# Append-only ledgers — union keeps both sides' appended rows (no false conflict)
*.jsonl            merge=union
improvement-log.md merge=union
